LEGEND:
  V = iso classes, T = total arc orbit transitions
  D = Burnside defect-1 count (Burnside-computable upper bound on SL_mine)
  SL_mine = actual self-loop orbit count
  D-SL = orbit size correction (from |Aut|>1 classes)
  non_SL = non-self-loop transitions = T - SL_mine
  2E = twice the number of simple edges
  surplus = non_SL - 2E = multi-edge surplus
  tw/D = fraction of D from 2-cycle types (twin contribution)

================================================================================
KEY FORMULAE (all Burnside-computable):
================================================================================

V(n) = (1/n!) sum_{ct all-odd} count(ct) * 2^{a(ct)}
T(n) = (1/n!) sum_{ct all-odd} count(ct) * 2^{a(ct)} * C(f(ct),2)
D(n) = (1/n!) sum_{ct with 1 even cycle 2k} count(ct) * k * 2^{a(ct)}

where a(ct) = sum(c//2) + sum(gcd(ci,cj)) and f(ct) = #{1-cycles}

RELATIONS:
  SL_mine <= D (equality iff all SL arc orbits have size 1)
  E <= (T - SL_mine)/2 (equality iff no multi-edges)
  E = (T - D + correction)/2 + multi_edge_correction

ASYMPTOTICS:
  D/V -> 0 (most classes have no self-loops)
  twin/D -> 1 (2-cycle types dominate)
  D ~ twin_SL ~ sum over k-cycles of k*2^{a(2,k^*)} terms

DONE.
